<http://data.silknow.org/object/9b89e57a-bff9-3373-8e53-0b1ba1be436b/observation/1>
        a                   crmsci:S4_Observation ;
        ecrm:P2_has_type    <http://data.silknow.org/observation/technical-observation> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note    "Panel of silk tapestry (<i>kesi</i>). At the top of the picture is a circular form containing two butterflies. The remainder of the picture is filled with water and rocks at the base, and exotic flowering plants filling the remainder of the picture. The panel may have been mounted as a hanging picture or as a wrapper for an important present.\nColours: gold thread, greens, blues, yellows, fawns, browns and pinks."@en ;
        crmsci:O8_observed  <http://data.silknow.org/object/9b89e57a-bff9-3373-8e53-0b1ba1be436b> .

